A||||23||theogre||Ogre notes||||6||
Z||000000||theogre||07-07-2000||04:18 PM||||For those of you who saw the other threads...... I'm still in Chemo. Today was last day of a full treatment week. back to one day treatment for next couple weeks.<P>So far other than losing the hair, I'm not doing to bad. Not getting allot of the fatigue many in chemo get, or not getting it baddly.<P>surgury scars are shrinking. I can get around better now. I still have to watch out for the blood clotting problem in my leg, but they tell me I'll always have to be carefull of that now. Apparently once you get one it damages the vien and you are prone to more of them latter. The alien (vien filter in chest) is supposed to catch any big stuff that breaks loose. (That was kind of fun to watch go in.... They do it in real time with a flouriscope. you can watch it moveing and then it pops out of the end of the tube. pretty bizar visual effect.||||reg||6
Z||000001||GT Bastard||07-07-2000||04:29 PM||||Hang in there man...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
